==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Jackie Peng]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 5.33~20 seconds<sup>160f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 13.33~26.67 seconds<sup>400f~800f</sup>.
*1 [[Master A.]] spawns after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>.
*1 [[Professor A.]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Project A]] spawns after 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
What's worse than one anteater? Three of them! Their combined DPS (especially if you haven't gotten most of the CotC treasures) will shred your meatshields and short-range attackers, so stall them with lots of meatshield spam and chip them away with [[:Category:Sniper-class Cats|snipers]] like [[Adult Cat (Rare Cat)|Prisoner Cat]] and [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Mina]]. Cash is plentiful thanks to the [[Celeboodle]]s, who also serve as great stepping stones for your Long Distance attackers—just make sure they don't advance too far and pick off your attackers, as their high strength magnifications are nothing to sneeze at.

[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] is an exceptional pick as it can use the peons to snipe the anteaters and clear the field for even more cash, greatly trivializing the stage. Disposable [[:Category:Waver-class Cats|Wavers]] like [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]] and [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Hermit Cat]] will also do well here, just take care to lure the peons away from the trio as without any stepping stones they will be as good as dead.

As far as {{4c}} strategies go, [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]] can hold the pair off fairly well for a short period of time, while additional meatshields like [[Carpenter Cat (Rare Cat)|Carpenter]] can support for your super backliners, particularly [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Mewtone]] if you have him.

